00:26:24,461 --> 00:26:26,560
Destined for demolition

363
00:26:26,561 --> 00:26:29,840
And be sorted out, sent back to the scrapyard

364
00:26:29,841 --> 00:26:31,420
And recycled

365
00:26:31,421 --> 00:26:34,240
As raw materials become scarce

366
00:26:34,241 --> 00:26:36,680
Recycling is bound to increase

367
00:26:36,681 --> 00:26:41,320
which is why the practice has become integral to the business of demolition.

368
00:26:42,840 --> 00:26:48,980
In Western Europe, they hope to mandate by the year 2010 that 100% of a building is recycled.

369
00:26:49,580 --> 00:26:55,900
In the United States, the industry continues to increase the volume of material that's recycled.

370
00:26:57,600 --> 00:26:59,840
There's no point in putting this material in a hole in the ground.

371
00:27:00,440 --> 00:27:01,360
There's money in it.

372
00:27:01,800 --> 00:27:02,900
It's good economic sense.

373
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:03,700
It's good business.

